# IMP-08 I-2: where each busy-Mac E2E file spends its time (DEC-002), before and after
# Commands: each file alone, one at a time: env -i PATH="$PATH" HOME=<new temp dir> TMPDIR="$TMPDIR" pnpm exec vitest run <file> --no-watch
#   --reporter=<phase reporter: each test's duration; console PHASE lines>, with temporary, uncommitted timers: each hook's
#   body wrapped in a timer, fetch calls over 200 ms logged, and for project-mutation-node-locality the fixture's migrate,
#   start and stop timed (the instrumentation scripts are reproduced at the end; files restored with git checkout afterwards).
# Busy-Mac emulation for the "stressed" runs: 16 CPU spinners and 8 file churners (write, rename, delete in a temp tree;
#   fseventsd reached ~60%, and a fresh fs.watch got no event within 20 s under it); stopped right after.
# Commits: before = 45ad9817e4 (I-1, I-3, I-4, I-5 done; I-2 not), after = 02ee9c2237 (I-2)
# Environment: macOS (Darwin 25.5.0), 10 cores, Node v22.23.1, vitest 4.1.12, built server from the worktree (pnpm build)
# Date: 2026-11-22
# The regime the failures came from (not reproducible here: fseventsd stays near 60% under any churn tried, and a recursive
#   fs.watch close took 0-2 ms): autobyteus-576 API-08b (load 8-12, fseventsd 166%) and autobyteus-583 API-07b (load 45-55,
#   fseventsd 140%). There the same files took 5-14 x their time here (node-locality 60 s, request-origin 31 s, provider-secret
#   28 s, embedding 18 s) and tests that answer in 5-120 ms timed out at 5 s.

